Each finding has exactly component, check, classification, assessment_tick,
proof. classification is consistent, violation or allowed_exception.
proof contains identity (source ref), alias (source ref), observed ({ref,value}),
observed_tick ({ref,value}), snapshot_tick ({ref,value}), baseline ({ref,value}),
rule (source ref), time_rule (source ref), exception (null or the object below).
For revision, baseline is the required revision; owner uses declared owner;
enabled uses the environment. The selected observation must be the latest
one admissible at the snapshot. Equality with a minimum meets that minimum.
identity must cite the component ID in its inventory document. alias must cite the alias-to-component
mapping in its inventory alias document, not an alias string from an observation. Both establish which
inventory component an observation belongs to. Use exact received source refs.
An owner exception is evaluated at the snapshot, not at observation time.
An applicable or expired owner exception has component (source ref), owner
({ref,value}), from_tick ({ref,value}), until_tick ({ref,value}), evaluated_at
(the snapshot tick), applies (boolean). Other checks use exception=null.
